               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding the discharge of your patient, a 57-year-old male, admitted on 15th May 1986 with acute right iliac fossa pain, nausea, and low-grade fever, clinically suspicious for appendicitis. Diagnostic workup including full blood count revealed elevated leukocytosis, and abdominal ultrasound confirmed appendiceal inflammation. A diagnosis of acute appendicitis was established. The patient underwent uncomplicated open appendectomy on 16th May 1986 under general anaesthesia. The postoperative course was uneventful, with no signs of wound infection or complications. Analgesia was managed with standard perioperative protocols, and the patient mobilised well. He was discharged home on 18th May 1986 in good general condition. Please ensure wound review in approximately one week and monitor for any signs of infection. Kind regards.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
